  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Soak the beans in water overnight and drain."
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the oil in a pan and saute the sliced onion for 5 minutes or until just starting to turn golden. Add the garlic and ginger paste and, when fragrant, add the chopped tomato, sliced green chilli, beans and ground spices and stir."
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour in water to cover plus 3 cm. Cover and cook over medium-low heat for about 2 hours or until the beans are soft. At this point you can partly blitz with a stick blender, but not to a completely smooth soup."
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt the butter in a pan and fry the finely chopped garlic, dried chillies and curry leaves for 1 minute. Add the cumin seeds and crushed mustard seeds and fry for another 5 seconds. Stir the contents of the pan into the beans."
    },
    {
      "text": "Ladle into bowls, add lemon juice and coriander and serve with rice."
    }
  ]
